---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="About | Prakhar Singh">
  <div class="prose max-w-none">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-8">About Me</h1>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-lg">
      <p>
        I am a doctoral student with an interest in solar physics at the
        Aryabhatta Research Institute of Observational Sciences (ARIES),
        Nainital, in joint coordination with IIT Roorkee. In December 2023, I
        began my PhD journey at ARIES, where I work with Dr. Vaibhav Pant on
        the exploration of solar coronal jets and associated small-scale
        flaring processes during Solar Cycle 24 and 25.
      </p>
      <p>
        I study the physics of the origin and evolution of solar jets using
        high spatio-temporal resolution data from the Extreme Ultraviolet
        Imager (EUI) on Solar Orbiter (SolO), IRIS, AIA/SDO, e-CALLISTO,
        XSM/Chandrayaan-2, and Aditya-L1.
      </p>
      <p>
        Prior to this, I pursued postgraduate studies at Banaras Hindu
        University, specializing in space physics, where I worked on
        studying lower ionosphere (D-layer) properties using very
        low-frequency waves.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
